Subject: [PATCH 4/8] test(ui): tiny-hole checkbox fills grey cracks and keeps
 white lines open (ADR-392)

Outside this package's files: TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx and
TraceCheckboxRow.tsx from main's #897, flagged for the integrator.

Operator change: the Fill tiny holes tooltip now reads "Fill grey
hairline cracks enclosed in solid ink. White lines and bright highlights
stay open; turn off to keep every crack. Open gaps always stay open." The
old text told operators to turn the box off to keep tiny highlights,
which the previous commit now keeps with the box on.

The semantic test still proves that the checkbox controls filling in Line
Art, Smooth and Sharp and that open gaps stay open. Its slits are now grey
(luma 160, just lighter than the cut) inside an ink block with a one-pixel
anti-aliased rim, as rasterised art has, and it adds the intended new
case: a slit as bright as the paper stays open with the box on. Before,
the test used pure white slits, which are drawn white lines under
ADR-392.

